cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Decision Rules for Streaming LLM Layers under Memory Pressure: Dense vs Mixture-of-Experts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bejaoui
    given-names: Abderrahmen
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/seneca-innovation-center/k8s-llm-offload-bench"
abstract: >-
  Measurements of five strategies for serving a language model larger than the free memory of a single
  Kubernetes node with one NVMe drive (cyclic multi-pod streaming, single-pod streaming, partial residency,
  kernel paging under a pod memory limit, speculative decoding on top of streaming), on six models
  (Qwen2.5-1.5B/3B/7B/14B, gpt-oss-20b, Qwen3-30B-A3B), 1,431 runs, bf16, no quantisation. Dense models are best
  served by single-pod streaming with tree speculation; mixture-of-experts models by kernel paging; no streaming
  scheme beats layer bytes divided by disk bandwidth.
keywords:
  - kubernetes
  - llm inference
  - offloading
  - mixture of experts
  - speculative decoding
